# cheat — local + remote cheatsheets
  cheat -h                    Show this help

## Local (your dotfiles)
  cheat                       List all local cheatsheets
  cheat <topic>               Show local cheatsheet; falls back to remote if not found
  cheat -e <topic>            Edit / create a local cheatsheet
  cheat -r <topic>            Force remote — useful when you have a local sheet
                              but want the cheat.sh version (e.g. cheat -r tmux)
  cheat -d <topic>            Download remote sheet to local downloads folder
  cheat -m                    Restore all sheets from downloads/.cheat-manifest
  cheat -s <keyword>          Search cheat.sh across all sheets

## Remote fallback: Unix/Linux commands
  cheat tar
  cheat rsync
  cheat curl

## Remote fallback: Language cheatsheets (lang/query namespace)
  cheat go/Pointers
  cheat python/lambda
  cheat js/"parse+json"       Use + for multi-word queries
  cheat go/"reverse+a+list"

## Remote fallback: Multiple answers (numbered)
  cheat python/"random+string"/1    First answer
  cheat python/"random+string"/2    Second answer

## Remote fallback: Language meta-queries
  cheat go/:list              List all topics for a language
  cheat go/:learn             Language primer ("Learn X in Y")
  cheat go/:random            Random page for a language

## Remote: Special pages
  cheat :help                 All special pages and options
  cheat :list                 List every available cheatsheet
  cheat :random               Random cheatsheet

## Downloaded cheatsheets (offline)
  cheat -d tar                Download tar sheet to topics/cheat/downloads/
  cheat tar                   Finds downloaded sheet automatically (no flag needed)

## tealdeer (tldr) — offline fallback, runs automatically
  tldr <cmd>                  Direct tealdeer lookup (bypasses cheat function)
  tldr --update               Refresh the local tldr cache (run periodically)
  tldr --list                 List all locally cached pages
  tldr --render <file.md>     Preview a local markdown file as a tldr page

## Query options (appended to remote URLs internally by cheat function)
  ?T                          Strip cheat.sh ANSI colors (bat re-colorizes)
  ?Q                          Strip comments, code only
  ?QT                         Both — clean code, no color, no comments
